WEBVTT

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.600
I guess it's summer
festival season already.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.260
I'm home, Soichiro.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.990
Welcome home. How did
today's interviews go?

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.330
So-so.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.740
Is that for me?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.520
Yes, it's from Grandma Yukari.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.240
That's great!

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.360
What is?

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.890
Thank you!

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.490
No!

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.150
S-Stop it!

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.110
Here.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.210
What's that?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.280
It's a cotton kimono.
What else?

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.860
That's nice. Just in time
for tomorrow's festival.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.300
I'm so busy with my
job hunt, I can't-

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.930
In this letter

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:52.560
she says she made the
white one for the manager.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.480
So they're a matching set.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.680
Godai, you have to go now.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.080
Thank you!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.870
Good morning.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.710
More job interviews?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.020
Yes, I'm going to three companies.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.550
Good luck.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:44.650
Thanks!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.020
I...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:48.260
Yes?

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.090
I want to thank you for the summer kimono.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.670
Did it fit you?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.300
Perfectly.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.930
I'm going to wear it tonight.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.510
I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.980
Oh? It's from Mitaka.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.280
A midsummer greeting to you!

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.240
Ms. Otonashi, I am a new man.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.520
I'd like to see you soon
regarding an important matter.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.220
"An important matter"?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.900
I wonder if he's
going to propose again?

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.510
What a cute dog.
But why a photo of a dog?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.170
Come on, McEnroe!

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.880
Good dog!

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.460
You big fat liar.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.060
I thought you were
deathly afraid of dogs.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.830
Uncle, are you familiar
with ninja training?

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.500
What're you talking about?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.830
In order to attain
superior jumping ability,

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:02.400
a ninja trains by jumping over a
growing seedling, day after day.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.580
Ultimately, he's able to leap over
a large tree in a single bound.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:10.500
So?

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.650
It's the same with dogs.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.910
If you get accustomed to one
from the time it's a pup...

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.620
My experiment was a success.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.060
That's great.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.590
Now, your chance
to get together

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.220
with dog-loving Asuna
is greatly improved.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.830
Let's not bring up
that musty old story.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.650
My goal is to be able
to pet one particular dog.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.510
I've put myself through
painfully tortuous training

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:41.510
day after day, just to be
able to pet one dog.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:11.730
Please let me find a job so
that I can propose to Kyoko.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.450
She's so sexy in that kimono.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.580
Hey, you two!

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:28.690
What did you pray for, Godai?

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.700
W-Well, for a job.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.960
That's it?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.630
O-Of course!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.020
Stand closer together,
you two.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.020
Okay.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.530
Grandma sure made
a good choice.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.200
You think so?

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.320
Please don't stare
like that.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.960
You look like
a husband and wife.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.100
Nah!

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.020
For now, anyway.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.760
Kentaro, do you want
to go play a game?

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.210
I wanna try the shooting game!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.220
Ma, I wanna eat a squid!
Buy me one?!

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.940
This... qualifies as a dog.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:27.620
I'm okay.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.150
I'm fine!

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:52.810
Shucks! Ma, can I
have another 100 yen?

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.000
No.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.810
You can use this, Kentaro.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:07:59.780
Thanks!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.070
Hi everyone.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:04.250
Mitaka.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.770
I dropped by your place,
but no one was home.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.960
I thought you might be here.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:11.920
I-I see.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.940
You're here, too, Godai?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.940
Ms. Otonashi, did
you get my letter?

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:22.060
Yes.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.370
What letter?

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.580
Where's Soichiro?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:32.120
Oh no! Where did Soichiro go?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.720
We must find him!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.770
Let's look for him!

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.150
Yes.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.940
I'll search that way!

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:46.520
Godai, you don't think Mitaka
got over his fear of dogs?

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.230
No way.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.660
We better look, too.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.660
It's pointless if we,
don't find Soichiro

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.010
or all my training
is for naught...

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:10.810
If Mitaka's no longer
afraid of dogs...

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.490
Mr. Godai!

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.220
Y-Yotsuya, why're you--?

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.090
This is an
extracurricular lesson.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.140
See? Don't we look great together?

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.900
I'm busy right now!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.550
Here!

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:14.900
I'm fine.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.730
Soichiro! There you are!

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:30.860
Soichiro!

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.700
Where were you, Soichiro?

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:46.300
We were worried about you.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.990
Mr. Mitaka, thank you so much.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.500
Ms. Otonashi.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.520
Y-Yes?

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.470
How dare he!

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.200
You found him! That's great.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.300
Yes.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.350
This can't be--!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.600
Ms. Otonashi, now do you
understand what I meant?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.400
Yes, I do.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:42.840
Great.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.670
Mitaka must have put
himself through a lot.

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:11.460
This pretty much decides it.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:18.180
Right. Now there's
nothing holding back Mitaka.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.960
On the other hand

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:24.780
his rival Godai hasn't
even found a job yet.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:31.470
Maybe Mitaka's going
to propose again soon.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.930
It's a possibility.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.830
What'll you do, Godai?

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.270
Don't give up.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:52.810
That's right! A man's gotta
rise to the challenge!

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.310
Mr. Godai! Look
what someone gave me.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.440
Who?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.650
Someone named Mitaka.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:01.580
Mitaka?

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:02.610
Hey.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.570
Cheers!

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.150
That's great!

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.050
This is the best!

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:27.550
Two more, please!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.730
Make that three!

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.070
Four!

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:31.340
What about you, Godai?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.780
Not yet.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.570
What's the matter?
Why so glum?

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.890
He's worried about
his job hunt.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.200
Let's not talk
about that tonight.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:49.290
He's got his eyes
on top-notch firms.

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:54.490
Top-notch firms?
You have connections!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.330
No, I don't!

00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:59.700
Can a graduate
of your college

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.550
get a job like that
without connections?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.550
D-Don't mock my school!

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:11.120
Yotsui and Mitsutomo
hire our graduates on merit alone,

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:13.190
...once every five years or so.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.320
Mitsutomo?

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.330
Let's talk about
something else.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.530
Godai, you want to work
for Mitsutomo Corporation?

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.770
If they hire me, sure.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.730
What're you smiling
about, Yagami?

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:35.680
My dad's the Director
of Recruiting there.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:37.240
What?

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.950
What if that were true, Mr. Godai?

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:52.060
What a cruel joke.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:55.620
Don't worry.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.600
Godai's that one guy
in five years

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.960
who'll get that job
without pulling strings.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.730
Are you being sarcastic?

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:06.410
Let's change the subject.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:11.370
Ms. Otonashi, is
that a new cotton kimono?

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:13.580
It's not the same one
you wore last year.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.020
You noticed?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:21.980
Godai's grandma
sent her that kimono.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:23.590
Huh?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.390
So it matches Godai's kimono.

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:32.790
Everyone told us we look
like a married couple.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:37.200
Did they tell you,
"for now"?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.810
How did you know?

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.410
Obviously, that's how
we all see it.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.940
Oh, no. He fell asleep.

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:12.280
Shall we call it a night?

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:13.040
Yes.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.810
Where's Yagami?

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.650
It's been a while
since I saw her.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.470
Maybe she went
to the restroom.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.210
But she's been gone
for a while.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.020
I'll see if I can find her.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.320
A firefly.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:58.420
Yagami? What's the matter?

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.950
I'm a little tired.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:03.630
I just came back from camp.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.810
You should loosen
your obi belt and relax.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:10.400
No! That'll lessen Mr. Godai's
chances of getting his job.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.870
You're not making any sense.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.370
My father is
a very strict man.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.610
I don't know what he'd think

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.730
if I came home with
my obi belt loosened.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:29.090
What's that have to do
with Godai's employment?

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:38.360
Is your father
really Mitsutomo's--?

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.450
I may be able to help him.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:44.670
My father never forgets a face.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.340
If only Mr. Godai could
give him a good impression.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:53.140
Yagami, I understand what
you're trying to do,

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.470
but think about it.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.610
He may have been

00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.450
a student-teacher at his
daughter's high school,

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.810
but that's no
real connection.

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:04.180
That's why I want him
to meet my father

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.540
and get to know each other
and establish a connection.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:08.830
Yagami!

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.420
Please don't worry about me.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.010
I'll have Mr. Godai
take me home.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:35.650
What? So what she said
about her Father was true?

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:36.930
Yes...

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.210
- Please stop.
- What?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.930
I could use any
help I can get,

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.930
but I'm not going to
take advantage of her.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.090
That's fine if that's
how you feel.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:52.100
But if your former student
isn't feeling well,

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:54.610
it's your duty to make sure
she gets home safely.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:03.850
It's not in me to try to
make an impression,

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.920
and if I did, it just
wouldn't be fair.

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.120
I'll just drop her off
in front of her door.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.850
Yagami, if you don't mind,
I'll say good-bye here.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:30.200
I'm sorry, Mr. Godai.
I really can't walk.

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:39.710
Mr. Godai, you need
to make a good impression.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.920
My father is
a very strict man.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.620
He hates people
who aren't proper.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:49.210
What're you talking about?
I'm not staying.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.920
Are you all right, Ibuki?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.050
Hello!

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.760
Your daughter
became ill, and-

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.960
Mr. Godai! This is my mother.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:02.000
There's no need to
get all tensed up.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.290
This isn't my father.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.760
You're Ibuki's tutor!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.870
Thank you so much
for your trouble.

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:11.530
Can he come in?

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.080
Thank you, but-

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.480
Please come in.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.380
Really, I-

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.210
You came all the way here.
Come in.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.020
You're home, Ibuki?

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:26.330
Dad!

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.700
And who's this?

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.930
He was a student-teacher
at Ibuki's school.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:35.410
My name is Yusaku Godai!
Please pardon my attire!

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:38.700
I started to feel sick and he was nice enough
to bring me home.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:45.470
Mr. Godai is interested in
finding a job at Mitsutomo.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.270
Hey!

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:47.040
But--

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:48.540
Don't say anything.

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:51.470
Why don't you change
and go to sleep?

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.390
Good luck.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.050
Go on.

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.520
So you're applying
for a job at Mitsutomo?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:03.560
Yes.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.530
But, um...

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.870
Please don't misunderstand.

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:12.180
This has nothing to do with my bringing
your daughter home.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:14.730
What do you mean?

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:18.030
I'm not here to network

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:22.780
and I don't expect you to be
impressed for my doing this.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.010
What's your name?

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:29.450
I'm Godai.

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:33.100
Godai, I'll remember you.

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:38.200
You may not be
the most polished,

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:42.290
but you show more promise than
a smooth-talking greenhorn.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:45.200
I'll see you
at the interview.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:47.800
Yes, sir! Good night!

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:56.510
Godai, huh?

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:11.430
I'm home!

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:17.030
Waiting for you!

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:19.110
How did it go with
the Director of Recruiting?

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:21.880
Not bad.

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:25.540
Your face says
things went well.

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:30.150
At the very least, I don't
think I left a bad impression.

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:31.880
That's great!

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.990
You're as good as hired!

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:36.400
It's too early for that.

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:38.900
We have to celebrate!

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:40.160
I agree!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:43.920
Let's drink again!
Bottoms up!

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.940
You're going
to drink some more?

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:55.000
I don't think they should
get their hopes up like that.

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:05.190
Ibuki? Shouldn't
you be resting?

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:07.810
I feel fine now.

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:10.830
Dad, get up.

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:12.810
Dad!

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:18.460
What did you think
of Mr. Godai?

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:21.960
Godai? Who's that?

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:26.560
Did you just get home, Ibuki?

00:23:26.950 --> 00:23:29.960
Huh? You don't
remember anything?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:35.150
It's no use. Your father's
been drunk all evening.

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:40.390
No...

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:48.900
Huh? Godai didn't
show up at the interview?

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:51.310
That idiot! How could he
miss a chance like that?!

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:53.600
Where the heck was he?

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:57.390
Next time:
"A Baby is Born:
Godai's Tearfully Happy Life!"

00:23:57.910 --> 00:23:59.350
A baby?!

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:02.130
You're going to give me
a heart attack!
